    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706-a1">

                <pb facs="1290" n="1166" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1166"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    430.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Council of Bourgeoisie of Neuveville to Mr.
                    Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Neuveville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 25,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Concerning the emigration of the woman
                    Olivier and her children, about whom we had the honor to write you on the 26th
                    of April last, and to which you had the kindness to reply, we take the liberty
                    to submit to you the inclosed declaration asking you to inform us whether, upon
                    the production of this document, the authorities <pb facs="1291" n="1167"
                        xml:id="pg1167"/> of New York will create difficulties to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">permit</hi> said woman to continue her journey to her
                    destination.</p>
                <p>You will excuse us, sir, hut desiring to allay the difficulties which might arise
                    concerning this family, we desire to he informed on this point.</p>
                <p>In begging you to accept our thanks in advance, we tender you the assurance of
                    our distinguished consideration.</p>
                <p>In the name of the Council of Bourgeoisie.</p>
                <p>The secretary.</p>
                <closer><signed>CESAR WYSS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
